.TH ACTIVITYTRACK-TUI 1 "November 2026" "activitytrack-tui 0.9.9" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
activitytrack-tui \- ActivityTrack in the terminal, full screen
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B activitytrack-tui
.RB [ \-\-data
.IR folder ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B activitytrack-tui
shows the activities running and the Home list of ActivityTrack (to-dos and
stopped activities) full screen, and works them from the keyboard. It is the
same application as the desktop tray application and the command line
.BR activitytrack (1),
on the same data and pairing: what they do shows within a second. The sync
runs in the background, every 30 seconds and after each change; after a sync
that did not go the next automatic one waits longer each time (30 seconds,
1, 2, then 5 minutes), until a change here or
.BR r .
To pair the
PC use the desktop application or
.BR "activitytrack pair" .
.SH KEYS
.TP
.BR "\(ua \(da" ", " j " " k
Move the selection.
.TP
.B Enter
The actions of the selected row, those its state allows: start (work or
travel), pause, resume, travel, stop, reopen (asks to confirm), done or
postpone a to-do, delete (into the bin) and restore. Each row shows the
symbol, the colour and the name of its state: to do, planned, late, work,
travel, pause, suspended, done, incomplete, absence, deleted.
.TP
.B n
A new one, of four kinds: to-do (title, client, priority from none to
emergency, plan and due date), work (description, client; now, already
started or past with start and end), travel, absence (company optional, kind
absence, holiday, leave or sickness, from and to day, optional times). In
the client list typing filters it; a new name becomes a new client when the
policy allows it.
.TP
.B t
A new to-do.
.TP
.BR p ", " s ", " v
Pause or resume, stop, travel the selected activity (or the one running).
Travel from work asks "Have you completed the work activity?"; stopping an
activity that went out and worked offers to start the return trip, to end
it, or to end it and add the return trip. There is no suspend command: an
activity is suspended when another one starts.
.TP
.B d
The selected to-do is done.
.TP
.BR f ", " g
The period and the states of the list.
.TP
.B r
Sync now.
.TP
.B a
Updates: asks the server this PC is paired with for a newer version. Its
announcement is signed and accepted only with the key of the pairing link
(a PC paired with an older link, or an announcement signed by another key,
is told why and offered nothing). The header shows a newer version known
from the last sync. The package is downloaded from the server and its
SHA-256 checked; an installation made by the package manager is told of the
new version but not offered the download, as the package manager updates
it.
.TP
.BR q ", " Esc
Quit; in a popup, close it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-data " folder"
Another data folder than the shared one.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/activitytrack/
The data shared with the desktop application and the command line.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/activitytrack/errors.log
Unexpected errors and warnings, as the desktop's.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR activitytrack (1)
.SH AUTHOR
The ActivityTrack contributors, https://gitlab.com/activitytrack/activitytrack-tui
